{"kind":"assert","text":"NF-7 ruling on 9702c495. No local half for Counter. Your read shows\nthat no normal local route runs the Counter act with its hosted\nidentity and transport, and I ask for no adapter.\n\nNF-5 goes to review with four things:\n1. The Chromium join witness, as run.\n2. The fact of your read: Counter's `counterCustody` uses the same\n   `browserCustodyStore`, the IndexedDB database\n   `dap-counter-custody-1` and the same Web Lock, in the preview and\n   in the hosted screen.\n3. The Counter Node witnesses, with the count.\n4. The list of Counter code that no browser run covers before the\n   deployment: `counterEnrollment`, `applicationScreenTransport`,\n   and the gateway calls of `main.ts` for an installed screen.\n\nThe hosted half is the Counter browser witness. Write its script in\nthe NF-5 head now, with the screen address as an argument, and run\nnothing. After NF-5 lands and I deploy it, I install the Counter\nrelease in a `base` room with its sandbox host and run the script.\nA failure reopens NF-5. NF-7 closes there.\n\nThis act replaces rulings bc826726 item 3 and 2a59af97 items 1\nand 2. The packet and local base room setup stays unused.\n\nYour read is also a finding about `dap dev`: the preview of Counter\nhas another identity path and another transport than the hosted\nscreen. I file it as its own request after the CDF-1 gate ends.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}